## The `help:` line for a `native.subset.1` problem (ADR 0722). The problem's
## message is written by `lower.ail` and its siblings; this file only reads it,
## so the messages can change without touching the lowering. A message with no
## entry here gets no help line. `owner` names the queued PR when the night-run
## merge order has one; `ail run` runs everything the backend refuses.

## The help text for a message, or "" when no entry matches. The first match
## wins, so the more specific forms come first.
pub fn subset_help(message str) str
    if message.contains("calling `TaskGroup`")
        or message.contains("Channel[")
        or message.contains("calling `Mutex`")
        or message.contains("`spawn`")
        return "tasks and channels aren't native yet (owner: #194); `ail run` runs them"
    if message.contains("maps")
        or message.contains("Map[")
        or message.contains("map comprehensions")
        return "maps aren't native yet (owner: #180); keep a `List` of pairs or a struct list, or use `ail run`"
    if message.contains("sets") or message.contains("set comprehensions")
        return "sets aren't native yet (owner: #180); use a `List` with a loop, or `ail run`"
    if message.contains("`==` on `str`") or message.contains("`!=` on `str`")
        return "string equality isn't native yet (owner: #184); compare the parts you need, or use `ail run`"
    if message.contains(".lines()")
        or message.contains("`.split()`")
        or message.contains("`.to_float()` on `str`")
        or message.contains("`.to_int()` on `str`")
        return "string methods beyond `chars` and `join` aren't native yet (owner: #184); `ail run` runs them"
    if message.contains("string interpolation outside `print`")
        return "interpolation is native only inside `print`; print the parts, or build the text with `xs.join(\", \")`"
    if message.contains("`?` on a") or message.contains("`?` with a context message")
        return "error values (`T ! E`) and `?` aren't native yet; return an optional `T?` or use `ail run`"
    if message.contains(".from_json")
        or message.contains("parse_json")
        or message.contains("`Json`")
        or message.contains("on a `Json`")
        return "JSON isn't native yet; `ail run` runs it"
    if message.contains("`bytes` literals") or message.contains("`env.find`")
        return "this isn't native yet (bytes and some std functions); `ail run` runs it"
    if message.contains("`char` patterns")
        return "`char` matches aren't native yet; compare with `==` in an `if`, or use `ail run`"
    if message.contains("error struct")
        or message.contains("error enum")
        or message.contains("unique struct")
        return "error and unique types aren't native yet; `ail run` runs them"
    if message.contains("attribute `@test`")
        return "tests aren't part of a native build; run them with `ail test` or `ail test --native`"
    if message.contains("methods of traits and `impl` blocks") or message.starts_with("trait `")
        return "traits and `impl` blocks aren't native yet (owner: #222); call the concrete functions instead"
    if message.contains("contracts aren't in the native subset yet")
        return "contracts aren't native yet; `ail run` checks them"
    if message.contains("`unsafe` blocks")
        return "unsafe blocks aren't native yet; `ail run` runs them"
    if message.contains("this `else` must leave")
        return "write `else return`, `else break`, `else continue`, or a fallback value"
    if message.contains("`for mut`")
        return "loop by index instead: `for i in 0..xs.len()` and `xs[i] = ...`"
    if message.contains("a comprehension whose element type isn't known")
        return "give the list its type with `List[T]()` and `push` in a loop"
    if message.contains(" on `?`")
        or message.contains("indexing a `?`")
        or message.contains("a `for` over a `?`")
        or message.contains("`.items` on `?`")
        or (message.contains("assigning `.") and message.contains("on `?`"))
        return "check the optional first with `if x := ...`; its fields, indexes and loops aren't native yet"
    if message.contains("`path` isn't in the native subset yet")
        or message.contains("isn't in the native subset yet (only locals, parameters and constants)")
        return "a module-level value that isn't a constant can't be read natively; pass it as a parameter"
    if message.contains("its result type isn't in the native subset yet")
        return "native results are int, float, bool, str, structs and enums, optionals and lists of those, or nothing"
    if message.contains("its type isn't in the native subset yet")
        return "native parameters and fields are int, float, bool, str, structs and enums, optionals and lists of those"
    if message.contains("printing a `")
        return "print the fields you need, for example `print(v.x)`"
    if message.contains("methods of `") and message.contains("aren't in the native subset yet")
        return "this method uses a construct outside the native subset; the other errors on it say which"
    if message.contains("generic functions")
        or message.contains("generic struct")
        or message.contains("generic enum")
        return "generics aren't native yet (owner: #219); write one function per type"
    return ""
